## WHATWG Encoding Standard — `index-*.txt` normative index tables

`src/testdata/index-*.txt` — one file for each of the 27 legacy single-byte
indexes of the Standard (ibm866, iso-8859-2..8 (-8-I shares iso-8859-8's), 10,
13..16, koi8-r, koi8-u, macintosh, windows-874, windows-1250..1258,
x-mac-cyrillic) — and `src/testdata/encodings.json` (the Standard's table of
encodings and labels) are vendored verbatim from the Encoding Standard published
at https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/, each index file's own header carrying
`Date: 2024-09-18` (the version fetched; `encodings.json` carries no date).
Each index is the normative byte-0x80..0xFF -> codepoint mapping for that code
page. Driven mechanically by `src/normative_vectors.zig` (parser),
`src/normative_test.zig` (the exhaustive 128-entry-per-page cross-check against
`root.zig`'s tables) and `src/sb_tables_test.zig` (the same for the generated
`src/sb_tables.zig`, plus the label table).

`src/sb_tables.zig` is GENERATED from these files by `tools/gen_tables.py` and is
a MODIFIED (reformatted, inverted, relabelled) rendering of their data — see the
modification indication below.

The Encoding Standard's own terms (`LICENSE` in the `whatwg/encoding`
repository, checked 2026-10-20; it is CC-BY 4.0 with BSD 3-Clause for portions
incorporated into source code — the vendored data files are covered by the
former):

