## simdjson — the "lookup" UTF-8 validation algorithm (`src/utf8_simd.zig`)

`src/utf8_simd.zig` ports, from simdjson's `src/generic/utf8_lookup4_algorithm.h`
(https://github.com/simdjson/simdjson, read 2026-10-20), the three 16-entry
nibble tables, their error-bit layout and the structure of the check — the
algorithm of J. Keiser and D. Lemire, "Validating UTF-8 In Less Than One
Instruction Per Byte", Software: Practice and Experience 51(5), 2021.
Modified: re-expressed in Zig vectors, with a portable select-tree lookup
beside `vpshufb`, a group-of-four error test, and a valid-prefix result
instead of a yes/no answer. simdjson is dual-licensed Apache-2.0 OR MIT; this
port is taken under MIT, whose notice follows verbatim (LICENSE-MIT, fetched
